 succeeded in 147ms:
Ticket: CHAOS-7132

A jira sync on the bigboy local org failed 0 of 14 units on 2026-09-29 and, behind it, nothing said why. The cause was already stored in the discovery ledger (`sync_run_reference_discoveries.result.detail`): `search atlassian teams: ... (/team/teamSearchV2) : Invalid Organization Ari: <uuid>`. The Atlassian Teams leg sent the organization as a bare UUID (tenantContexts answers a bare UUID) and the gateway wants the ARI form; the leg runs strict inside reference discovery, so its failure failed every unit of a sync that does not depend on it.

## What changes
- `atlassianteams.Collect` sends the organization as `ari:cloud:platform::org/<uuid>` (an id that already is an ARI is unchanged).
- BEHAVIOUR CHANGE (D3666, D2778): the Atlassian Teams leg is additive. In strict reference discovery its failure no longer fails discovery or any unit. It is never silent and never a clean success: Warn line, dispatch outcome `native_failed_nonfatal`, discovery ledger outcome `native_degraded` with `degraded: [{dataset, leg, outcome, reason, detail}]`, and the same entry in `sync_runs.result` (the run status stays what its units compute; no `partial_failed`). The strict CLI verb `dho sync teams --provider jira` still exits non-zero when the leg fails (there the leg is the work).
- `ErrCredentialInvalid` stops being one bare sentinel: each source now carries a fixed, value-free reason (`encryption_key_not_configured`, `decrypt_failed`, `payload_not_a_json_object`, `ciphertext_missing`, `provider_mismatch`, `credential_id_mismatch`, jira `missing_fields:<names>`), all still `errors.Is(ErrCredentialInvalid)`. `providerfoundation.FailureReason` gives the word for a durable row; unit and run results of a discovery failure carry it as `reason`.
- Every error the post-sync team-catalog seam drops now leaves a Warn (org, run, provider, stage, error); the skipped Atlassian leg (no client base URL) is logged; the worker's credential-cipher refusal names its reason.
- `dho sync teams --provider jira` resolves the credential the org's jira integration points at (as the worker does), refuses two integrations with different credentials, and refuses up front without SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY.

## Timeline (bigboy, local org)
Jira sync (integration 57d1c4ff) succeeded 14/14 on 08-31 and on 2026-09-28 03:06Z and 05:10Z, then failed 0/14 on 2026-09-29 01:38Z (first run after rev 197). The Atlassian leg was wired into the worker's team-catalog collector by #3357 (CHAOS-7002, merged 09-27 20:00Z) and made to reach the gateway by #3365 (CHAOS-7020, live organization-id resolution, merged 09-28 05:47Z); the failing run is the first on a build with both. Earlier D3124 readings ("credential invalid", "the worker has a working client") are superseded: the stored payload has all three required fields (names/booleans probe, executed), and current code accepts it.

## Boot-time key check (which processes)
worker sync/provider families refuse to start without the key (provider_sync.go:641, sync_dispatch.go:447/451/563; now log the reason); stream runner refuses (streamrunnerservice/dependencies.go:199-207); sync CLI now refuses for jira; scheduler keeps running with source discovery and credential-fingerprint stamping disabled and logs the error (schedulerservice/dependencies.go:417-430, intentional, now names the reason); api leaves the decryptor zero and the PagerDuty route answers 500 at request time (apiservice/deps.go:342, documented).

## TEST-EVIDENCE
- Red on the untouched baseline, then green: jira refusal names the missing fields; resolver reasons; dropped client/collector error logs; skipped-leg log; strict collection keeps the catalog when the Atlassian leg fails (red: `provider sync configuration is invalid` returned as an error); organization as ARI (red: bare UUID passed); CLI resolves the integration's credential (red: picked the credential named default); two integrations refused; finalize copies the ledger's degraded legs (red with the copy disabled: `{"completed_units":1,"failed_units":0}`).
- Readers of `sync_runs.result` pinned: the sync-run response passes `degraded` through; the sync handoff's key-targeted read ignores it.
- `go test` of providerfoundation, providersync, workerservice, syncdispatchruntime, scheduler/..., schedulerservice, streamrunnerservice, api/..., synccli, atlassianteams: ok; integration tests for the CLI scope, the handoff reader and the finalize copy: ok.

## RISK-NOTES
- `DegradedLeg.Detail` is `err.Error()`, persisted in the ledger and copied into `sync_runs.result`, bounded to 500 bytes and sanitized by the recorder (the same `sanitizeErrorText` the discovery failure detail uses). For a provider failure that is class, status and request path only (`ProviderError.Error` never formats the response body: pinned by a test with a body fragment); for the gateway's GraphQL errors it is the gateway's own message, which can carry the organization id (an identifier, not a secret).
- `siteId` (the raw cloud UUID) sent to `teamSearchV2` is NOT proven by any live call: the gateway only rejected the organization. The real post-merge run proves it; if it is also refused the degraded entry will say so.
- No surface shows the degraded entry to a user yet (follow-up filed: the sync status API and data-health view show a degraded dataset). The data is in `sync_runs.result.degraded` and the ledger.
- `sync_runs.result` gains `reason` (a unit's fixed reason) and `degraded`; the zero-unit branch already used `reason` for its own fixed word.
- Not done here: the decrypt of a credential in a process with the wrong salt/key still reads `decrypt_failed` (it cannot tell wrong key from tampering).


